%% Logical sequence, Store includes reconstruction, journaling, and project files.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Developer
    participant UI as CLI / cascade loop
    participant S as Session
    participant P as Planner / review
    participant Q as Scheduler / locks
    participant A as Runner / adapters
    participant V as Conflict detector
    participant N as Store / files / Git

    User->>UI: Submit task (or --recover)
    UI->>S: Initialize / recover
    S->>S: Acquire exclusive project lease
    S->>N: Recover interrupted commit journal
    alt New task
        S->>N: Ingest / reconcile source files and node store
        S->>P: Build dependency context, request a subtask plan
        P-->>S: Subtasks, dependencies, read / write targets
        S->>S: Validate plan against code dependencies
        opt Initial plan review enabled
            S->>User: Display plan for approval / editing
            User-->>S: Approve plan (abort ends run)
        end
        S->>Q: Install DAG and persist task graph
    else Resume interrupted run
        S->>Q: Clear stale leases, restore DAG and incomplete work
    end

    loop While runnable work remains and run limits permit
        S->>Q: Tick ready queue
        Q->>Q: Check worker capacity, acquire all required locks
        Note over Q,A: Contended tasks wait, independent tasks run concurrently
        Q->>A: Dispatch task through Session's bounded worker pool
        A->>S: Enrich TaskBundle, check context and token budgets
        S->>N: Read current targets and dependency context
        N-->>S: Granted source fragments + read-only context
        S-->>A: Enriched TaskBundle
        A->>A: Call configured API or CLI adapter
        Note over S,Q: Heartbeat renews in-flight leases, watchdog checks deadlocks
        A-->>S: TaskResult with returned source fragments
        Note over S,N: Collect completions in batches, apply in deterministic DAG order
        S->>N: Stage returned fragments within task grants
        S->>V: Check staged edits against batch peers
        V-->>S: Compile and structural-check report
        S->>N: Assemble and compile prospective affected files
        S->>Q: Revalidate write-lock ownership
        alt Validation passes and locks are held
            S->>N: Begin transaction, advance node versions in memory
            N->>N: Render all files, journal backups, replace files atomically
            alt File installation and metadata save succeed
                N-->>S: Durable transaction committed
                S->>N: Record optional Git audit commit, finalize journal
                S->>Q: Release completed grants, complete task or narrow remainder
                Q->>Q: Persist progress, unblock dependent tasks
            else Transaction fails before commit point
                N->>N: Restore files and store snapshot
                S->>Q: Release locks, retry within limits or mark failed
            end
        else Invalid result, conflict, or lost lock
            S->>N: Discard staged versions
            S->>Q: Release locks, retry within limits or mark failed
        end
        Note over S,Q: Agent / transport failures also enter bounded retry handling
    end
    S-->>UI: Initial wave result

    loop Post-wave check, bounded by cascade wave limit
        UI->>S: Detect broken callers and cross-module API defects
        S-->>UI: Fix-up tasks, or none
        opt Fix-up tasks found
            UI->>User: Review proposed fix-up plan
            User-->>UI: Approve / edit / decline
            opt Plan approved
                UI->>S: Install approved plan and run the same execution loop
                S-->>UI: Fix-up wave result
            end
        end
        Note over UI,S: Stop when clean, declined, or limit reached, retain unresolved work
    end

    UI->>S: Teardown with aggregate execution outcome
    S->>S: Run configured tests: passed / failed / skipped / error
    opt auto_push enabled, request satisfied, and test policy met
        S->>N: Push Git audit history
    end
    S-->>UI: Test outcome and push result
    UI->>S: Close workers and release project lease
    UI-->>User: Report completed, failed, blocked, and unresolved work
